# `vite build --mode e2e`, which is what `pnpm e2e` builds (playwright.config.ts).
#
# `backend.md` B1 moved /api/ask, /api/examples and /api/recall out of this app
# and into `apps/server`, and deleted the dev/preview adapter that used to mount
# them on the app's own origin. So the e2e build has to be told where the API
# is, exactly as a deployment is (docs/deploy.md §4) — and the value is a
# DIFFERENT ORIGIN on purpose: that is what makes `pnpm e2e` exercise the CORS
# preflight and the `X-Tangram-Access` header the way a browser will in
# production. A same-origin run proves none of it (`web.md` R10).
#
# 127.0.0.1 rather than localhost so the app origin (http://localhost:<PORT>)
# and the API origin are unambiguously different to the browser.
# `playwright.config.ts` starts the server on this port and puts the app's
# origin in its allowlist.
VITE_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8787
